# Temporary Access Pass (TAP)

A Temporary Access Pass is a temporary authentication credential that can be used to help a user register authentication methods or recover access when their normal strong authentication method is unavailable.

TAP settings used in this lab:

- Duration: 1 hour
- One-time use: Yes
- Delayed start: No

The TAP was enabled by the authentication policy.

---

# TAP Troubleshooting

During the lab, the TAP appeared to have an incorrect/old expiration time.

Investigation showed that the Windows workstation was configured with:

- Incorrect timezone: Pacific Time (UTC-08:00)
- Automatic time synchronization: Off
- Last successful synchronization: January 5, 2026

The workstation was corrected to:

- Timezone: West Central Africa (UTC+01:00)
- Automatic time synchronization: On
- Time synchronized with `time.windows.com`

This demonstrated an important troubleshooting principle:

> Always verify the endpoint's date, time and timezone when investigating authentication or timestamp-related problems.

